Chapter: PinochleWasm
  cites Games chapter Pinochle
  cites Games chapter Rng
  cites Foreword chapter List

 The browser interface for Pinochle, on the handle contract in
 games-backlog.md GAME-11. Four twelve-card hands and the trump are past an
 i32, so the page holds the state's address.

 The deal and the result are separate handles because a page shows the
 hands before it shows a score.

 You are seat 0 and you lead the first trick, which is why nothing here has
 to advance the play before handing the page a handle. `pn-wasm-play` takes
 an index into YOUR OWN hand rather than a card id: a pinochle deck holds
 two of every card, so a card id does not name a card in a hand.

 Nothing in this chapter writes through `list-set-at`. A play answers a
 fresh record whose hands are built by `pin-remove-at` onto an empty
 accumulator, so a handle a page is holding stays the position it was.

 We say:

Section: The Browser Interface

  pn-wasm-new : Integer -> PinochleState
  pn-wasm-new (seed) = pin-deal (pin-shuffle pin-deck-new (rng-new seed))

  pn-wasm-trump : PinochleState -> Integer
  pn-wasm-trump (st) = st.trump

  pn-wasm-hand : PinochleState, Integer -> List Integer
  pn-wasm-hand (st) (player) =
    if player == 0 then st.h0
    else if player == 1 then st.h1
    else if player == 2 then st.h2
    else st.h3

  pn-wasm-card : PinochleState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pn-wasm-card (st) (player) (i) =
    if player < 0 then (-1)
    else if player >= 4 then (-1)
    else if i < 0 then (-1)
    else let hand = pn-wasm-hand st player
    in if i >= list-length hand then (-1)
    else list-at hand i

  pn-wasm-meld : PinochleState, Integer -> Integer
  pn-wasm-meld (st) (player) =
    if player < 0 then (-1)
    else if player >= 4 then (-1)
    else score-meld (pn-wasm-hand st player) (st.trump)

  pn-wasm-count : PinochleState, Integer -> Integer
  pn-wasm-count (st) (player) =
    if player < 0 then 0
    else if player >= 4 then 0
    else list-length (pn-wasm-hand st player)

  pn-wasm-cur : PinochleState -> Integer
  pn-wasm-cur (st) = st.turn

  pn-wasm-leader : PinochleState -> Integer
  pn-wasm-leader (st) = st.leader

  pn-wasm-trick : PinochleState, Integer -> Integer
  pn-wasm-trick (st) (seat) =
    if seat < 0 then (-1)
    else if seat >= 4 then (-1)
    else pin-played st seat

  pn-wasm-legal : PinochleState, Integer -> Integer
  pn-wasm-legal (st) (idx) = if pin-legal st idx then 1 else 0

  pn-wasm-play : PinochleState, Integer -> PinochleState
  pn-wasm-play (st) (idx) = pin-play-at st idx

  pn-wasm-step : PinochleState -> PinochleState
  pn-wasm-step (st) = pin-step st

  pn-wasm-done : PinochleState -> Integer
  pn-wasm-done (st) = if st.done then 1 else 0

  pn-wasm-tricks : PinochleState -> Integer
  pn-wasm-tricks (st) = st.tricks

  pn-wasm-pts : PinochleState, Integer -> Integer
  pn-wasm-pts (st) (team) = if team == 0 then st.t0 else st.t1

  pn-wasm-run : Integer -> PinochleResult
  pn-wasm-run (seed) = run-pinochle-hand seed

  pn-wasm-t0 : PinochleResult -> Integer
  pn-wasm-t0 (r) = r.team0-score

  pn-wasm-t1 : PinochleResult -> Integer
  pn-wasm-t1 (r) = r.team1-score

  pn-wasm-winner : PinochleResult -> Integer
  pn-wasm-winner (r) = r.winner

